<p><strong>New benchmark shows how AI models lack intuitive visual reasoning:<br /></strong><em>…Humanity’s Sixth Sense highlights some shortcomings of current AI systems…<br /></em>AI startups Elorian and Scale AI have built and released Humanity’s Sixth Sense, a benchmark that “measures how a model interprets and reasons through information a visual scene implies but doesn’t explicitly show.” Some examples of the types of task in HSS are a picture of a bookcase and being asked whether it can fit more books, or a photo of horses pulling a plough and a question of whether the chains bear the plough’s drag weight. </p>
<p><strong>HSS contains </strong>522 questions that cover 288 images and 234 short video clips (totalling 17.6 hours of video). The questions fall into four categories:</p>
<ul>
